# A copy through a result field written under an if, one struct down (#125):
# v1_0.s.a is v0_0.n only where v0_0.k == "x", so v1_0.b is not a copy of
# v0_0.n everywhere.
-- source.cue --
k: "x" | "y"
n: int32
-- target.cue --
s: {a?: int32}
b!: int32
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	s: {if v0_0.k == "x" {a: v0_0.n}}
	b: v1_0.s.a
}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.b reads v1_0.s.a, which is written only under v0_0.k == "x", and the checker cannot show that holds wherever v1_0.b is written; write v1_0.b under the same patterns, or v1_0.s.a on every path (rule unknown-exhaustive) @ lens.cue:4:5
